Optional text memo for pczt_create

Applies on top of 0001-sync-progress.patch.

WebWallet.pczt_create(account_id, to_address, value, memo?) takes an optional
UTF-8 text memo for the recipient. It is encoded as ZIP 302 MemoBytes (at most
512 bytes; longer text fails with Error::MemoTooLong) and the payment is built
with zip321::Payment::new, which returns None for a memo to an address that
cannot receive one (transparent P2PKH/P2SH, TEX, or a unified address with only
a transparent receiver); that fails with upstream's own
Error::UnsupportedMemoRecipient, as ZIP 321 requires. An empty string is the
same as no memo, and callers that pass three arguments keep the old behaviour
(Payment::without_memo).

The request is now built before the chain-tip check and the inline sync in
pczt_create, so an invalid memo or recipient is rejected at once.

